</Fragment>
<style is:global>
  *, *::before, *::after { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  :root {
    --orange: #FF5500; --orange-hover: #E84A00; --orange-pale: #FFF3EE;
    --black: #111111; --white: #FFFFFF; --off-white: #FAFAF8;
    --gray: #F4F4F2; --border: #E8E8E5; --text-muted: #777; --nav-h: 72px;
  }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body { font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; background: var(--white); color: var(--black); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden; }

  /* PAGE HEADER */
  .page-header { padding-top: var(--nav-h); background: var(--black); }
  .page-header-inner { padding: 72px 48px 0; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .page-header-inner::before { content: 'PACK'; position: absolute; top: 0; right: -10px; font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 220px; letter-spacing: 8px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); pointer-events: none; line-height: 1; }
  .breadcrumb { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--orange); text-decoration: none; }
  .page-header-inner h1 { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: clamp(52px, 7vw, 92px); letter-spacing: 3px; color: var(--white); line-height: 0.9; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .page-header-inner h1 span { color: var(--orange); }
  .page-header-inner > p { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); max-width: 560px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .header-stats { display: flex; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); margin-top: 48px; }
  .header-stat { flex: 1; padding: 20px 32px; border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); }
  .header-stat:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .header-stat-num { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 36px; color: var(--orange); letter-spacing: 2px; line-height: 1; }
  .header-stat-label { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3); margin-top: 3px; }

  /* SECTIONS */
  .section { padding: 80px 48px; }
  .section-alt { background: var(--off-white); }
  .section-dark { background: var(--black); color: var(--white); }
  .label { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--orange); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .label-dark { color: rgba(255,165,0,0.8); }
  h2 { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 58px); letter-spacing: 2px; line-height: 0.95; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .lead { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.7; color: #444; max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .lead-dark { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); }

  /* WHAT IS A CO-PACK */
  .what-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: start; }
  .what-left { max-width: 560px; }
  .what-left p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: #444; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .what-right { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
  .callout-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--orange); padding: 20px 24px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .callout-card h4 { font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .callout-card p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* FORMATS GRID */
  .formats-intro { max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .formats-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
  .format-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 28px 24px; transition: box-shadow 0.2s, transform 0.2s; }
  .format-card:hover { box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .format-icon { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 32px; color: var(--orange); letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1; }
  .format-card h3 { font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .format-card p { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .format-tag { display: inline-block; margin-top: 14px; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--gray); color: var(--text-muted); padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .format-tag.manual { background: #EDFBF0; color: #2d7a47; }
  .format-tag.equipment { background: #FFF3EE; color: var(--orange); }

  /* RTS SECTION */
  .rts-section { background: var(--black); padding: 80px 48px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .rts-section::before { content: 'RTS'; position: absolute; bottom: -40px; right: -20px; font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 300px; letter-spacing: 8px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); pointer-events: none; line-height: 1; }
  .rts-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .rts-left h2 { color: var(--white); }
  .rts-left p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .rts-stat-row { display: flex; gap: 40px; margin-top: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .rts-stat { border-left: 2px solid var(--orange); padding-left: 16px; }
  .rts-stat-num { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 40px; color: var(--orange); letter-spacing: 2px; line-height: 1; }
  .rts-stat-label { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3); margin-top: 3px; }
  .rts-right { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  .rts-card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius: 6px; padding: 24px; }
  .rts-card h4 { font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .rts-card p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); }

  /* WHY SECTION */
  .why-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 32px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .why-card { padding: 32px 28px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; }
  .why-num { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 48px; color: rgba(255,85,0,0.15); letter-spacing: 2px; line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .why-card h3 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .why-card p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* PROCESS */
  .process-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 0; margin-top: 48px; position: relative; }
  .process-row::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 28px; left: 10%; right: 10%; height: 1px; background: var(--border); z-index: 0; }
  .process-step { text-align: center; position: relative; z-index: 1; padding: 0 12px; }
  .step-num { width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--orange); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: 22px; color: var(--white); letter-spacing: 1px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .process-step h4 { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .process-step p { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* CTA */
  .page-cta { background: var(--orange); padding: 80px 48px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .page-cta::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: -80px; right: -80px; width: 400px; height: 400px; border: 80px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius: 50%; }
  .page-cta-inner { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; position: relative; z-index: 1; gap: 40px; }
  .page-cta h2 { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive; font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); letter-spacing: 3px; color: var(--white); line-height: 0.9; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .page-cta p { font-size: 16px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); max-width: 440px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .btn-white { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: var(--white); color: var(--orange); font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 14px 28px; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; transition: transform 0.15s; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .btn-white:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .btn-outline-white { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: transparent; color: var(--white); border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-family: 'Barlow', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; transition: border-color 0.2s, color 0.2s; margin-top: 16px; }
  .btn-outline-white:hover { border-color: var(--white); color: var(--white); }

  .fade-up { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(28px); transition: opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease; }
  .fade-up.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  .delay-1 { transition-delay: 0.1s; }
  .delay-2 { transition-delay: 0.2s; }
  .delay-3 { transition-delay: 0.3s; }
  .delay-4 { transition-delay: 0.4s; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .section { padding: 56px 24px; }
    .rts-section { padding: 56px 24px; }
    .page-header-inner { padding: 48px 24px 0; }
    .header-stats { flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .header-stat { min-width: 50%; }
    .what-grid, .rts-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .formats-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .why-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .process-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .process-row::before { display: none; }
    .page-cta { padding: 60px 24px; }
    .page-cta-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .formats-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .process-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rts-stat-row { gap: 24px; }
  }
</style>

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="page-header">
  <div class="page-header-inner">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/pages/services">Services</a> / Co-Pack Assembly</div>
    <h1>CO-PACK <span>ASSEMBLY</span><br>SINGAPORE</h1>
    <p>Promotional packs built fast — stickering, GWP attachment, shrink bundling, multi-pack banding and kitting. Warehouse space and manpower included. Brief us, we build it.</p>
    <div class="header-stats">
      <div class="header-stat"><div class="header-stat-num">48–72h</div><div class="header-stat-label">Typical Turnaround</div></div>
      <div class="header-stat"><div class="header-stat-num">10+</div><div class="header-stat-label">Assembly Formats</div></div>
      <div class="header-stat"><div class="header-stat-num">SG-based</div><div class="header-stat-label">Warehouse & Team</div></div>
      <div class="header-stat"><div class="header-stat-num">End-to-end</div><div class="header-stat-label">Assemble → Deploy</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHAT IS A CO-PACK -->
<section class="section fade-up">
  <div class="what-grid">
    <div class="what-left">
      <div class="label">What is a Co-Pack</div>
      <h2>THE PROMOTIONAL SKU YOUR RETAILER ACTUALLY WANTS</h2>
      <p>A co-pack — also known as a deal pack or promotional SKU — is a specially assembled version of an existing product engineered for a specific retail channel or promotional window. It carries its own barcode (EAN), its own shelf price, and its own pack format.</p>
      <p>Brand owners use co-packs to hit a price point that drives trial and volume without discounting the mainline SKU — protecting margin while giving the retailer a compelling listing reason. Channels like NTUC FairPrice, Cold Storage, Giant, Sheng Siong and Guardian all routinely require channel-specific co-packs as a condition of promotional slots.</p>
      <p>In Singapore, co-packs are typically assembled in-market — often at short notice — rather than built in a factory overseas. That's where Elitez comes in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="what-right">
      <div class="callout-card fade-up delay-1">
        <h4>Price-point engineering</h4>
        <p>Bundle two units at S$6.90 without touching the S$3.95 mainline price — the co-pack carries a new EAN and a new retail price, protecting both the brand and the retailer's margin.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="callout-card fade-up delay-2">
        <h4>Retailer listing leverage</h4>
        <p>A retailer-exclusive co-pack gives buyers a reason to accept a secondary off-shelf location — end-of-aisle, gondola end, or freestanding display — at no extra ranging cost to the brand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="callout-card fade-up delay-3">
        <h4>In-market speed</h4>
        <p>Campaign windows are short. Assembling co-packs in Singapore means you can brief us on Monday and have retail-ready packs on shelf by Thursday — no factory lead time, no cross-border shipment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ASSEMBLY FORMATS -->
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="label">What We Build</div>
  <h2 class="fade-up">10+ CO-PACK <span style="color:var(--orange)">ASSEMBLY FORMATS</span></h2>
  <div class="formats-intro fade-up">
    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#444;">From a single promotional sticker to a fully shrink-bundled multi-pack, our warehouse team handles the full spectrum of co-pack assembly without factory-level machinery. Here's what we build.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="formats-grid">
    <div class="format-card fade-up">
      <div class="format-icon">01</div>
      <h3>Promotional Stickering</h3>
      <p>Hand-applied or semi-auto label application — price flash stickers, "Win More" mechanics, bonus pack callouts, QR codes, and contest entry stickers. Applied at up to 1,800 units/hr with a label applicator.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual / Semi-auto</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="format-icon">02</div>
      <h3>Multi-pack Banding</h3>
      <p>Bundling 2, 3 or 6 units together with a self-adhesive band or printed polypropylene strap — the standard format for "Buy 2 Get 1 Free" and twin-pack mechanics in Singapore supermarkets.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="format-icon">03</div>
      <h3>GWP Attachment</h3>
      <p>Securing a gift-with-purchase item — a premium, travel-size sample, or branded accessory — to the primary product using adhesive dots, rubber bands, stretch film, or a polybag carry. Clean, retail-ready finish.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-3">
      <div class="format-icon">04</div>
      <h3>Shrink Bundling</h3>
      <p>L-bar sealer + shrink tunnel: multiple units wrapped in clear or printed shrink film into a single retail-ready pack. The standard for bottled beverages, personal care multi-packs, and condiment twins.</p>
      <span class="format-tag equipment">Equipment: Shrink Tunnel</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up">
      <div class="format-icon">05</div>
      <h3>Tray + Shrink Packs</h3>
      <p>Product placed into a printed or plain corrugated tray then shrink-wrapped — a retail display-ready format common for NTUC gondola ends and freestanding display units (FSDUs).</p>
      <span class="format-tag equipment">Equipment: Shrink Tunnel</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="format-icon">06</div>
      <h3>Neck Tag & Collar Application</h3>
      <p>Hanging promotional leaflets, contest mechanics, premium tags or paper collars around bottle necks and product tops — a high-visibility callout with zero impact on the primary packaging.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="format-icon">07</div>
      <h3>Gift Set Kitting</h3>
      <p>Assembling multi-SKU gift sets into a carrier bag, window box, or clamshell — common for CNY, Hari Raya, and Deepavali gifting mechanics across personal care, food and beverage brands.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-3">
      <div class="format-icon">08</div>
      <h3>Carded Pack Assembly</h3>
      <p>Securing product to a printed backing card using tape, adhesive, or cable ties — a clean, cost-effective format for impulse POS display and checkout counter fixtures in convenience and pharmacy.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up">
      <div class="format-icon">09</div>
      <h3>Polybag + Header Card</h3>
      <p>Product inserted into a clear polybag with a printed header card — a versatile retail-hanging format for pharmacy, convenience and specialist channels. Quick to assemble at scale.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="format-icon">10</div>
      <h3>Clip Strip Loading</h3>
      <p>Loading individual SKUs or GWP premiums onto plastic clip strips for hanging point-of-purchase displays. Strips are rack-ready for supermarket aisles, pharmacy shelving, and convenience counter units.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="format-icon">11</div>
      <h3>Price-Marked Pack (PMP) Labelling</h3>
      <p>Applying retail price-marked labels to existing stock for channel-specific pricing — common for convenience and petrol mart channels where pre-priced product reduces friction at the counter.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">Manual / Semi-auto</span>
    </div>
    <div class="format-card fade-up delay-3">
      <div class="format-icon">12</div>
      <h3>On-site Assembly</h3>
      <p>Can't bring product to our warehouse? We bring the team to yours. Our manpower can mobilise to your facility or a third-party warehouse anywhere in Singapore for large-volume or time-critical runs.</p>
      <span class="format-tag manual">On-site</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- RTS SECTION -->
<section class="rts-section">
  <div class="rts-grid">
    <div class="rts-left">
      <div class="label label-dark">The 2027 Pressure</div>
      <h2 style="color:var(--white);">WHAT THE JB–SG RTS LINK MEANS FOR <span style="color:var(--orange)">YOUR BRAND</span></h2>
      <p>The Johor Bahru–Singapore Rapid Transit System opens in January 2027. Grocery prices in JB run 20–40% below Singapore retail. When the commute becomes a 7-minute train ride, buying detergent, personal care and snacks across the border stops being inconvenient.</p>
      <p>An independent study projects S$1.05 billion in annual Singapore consumer spend moving to JB once the link opens — with groceries the single largest category. The non-perishables most at risk are exactly the categories where FMCG brands spend on promotions: laundry, personal care, beverages, snacks, canned goods.</p>
      <p>The defensive play is not a price war. It is value-perception mechanics: exclusive bundle packs, GWP promotions, in-store activations, and retail-specific co-packs that give Singapore shoppers a reason to buy here. That means more co-packs, shorter lead times, and faster promotional cycles — starting now, before January 2027.</p>
      <div class="rts-stat-row">
        <div class="rts-stat">
          <div class="rts-stat-num">S$1.05B</div>
          <div class="rts-stat-label">Projected Annual Leakage</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rts-stat">
          <div class="rts-stat-num">+51%</div>
          <div class="rts-stat-label">SG Trips to JB Post-RTS</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rts-stat">
          <div class="rts-stat-num">Jan 2027</div>
          <div class="rts-stat-label">RTS Link Opens</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rts-right">
      <div class="rts-card">
        <h4>The categories most at risk</h4>
        <p>Non-perishables with low brand loyalty and high price sensitivity: laundry detergents, personal care (shampoo, body wash), beverages (RTD, instant coffee), snacks and condiments. These are the exact categories where co-pack promotions drive the strongest trial and repeat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rts-card">
        <h4>Why co-packs are the right defensive tool</h4>
        <p>A retailer-exclusive bundle at a channel price point gives Singapore shoppers perceived value that a JB grocery run can't easily replicate — especially when paired with a GWP or loyalty mechanic. Price arbitrage loses when the pack itself isn't available across the border.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rts-card">
        <h4>Start building your RTS-defence promo calendar now</h4>
        <p>The brands that will hold market share post-RTS are the ones running promotional cadences in H2 2026 and Q1 2027 — not reacting after the traffic data changes. Elitez can help you build the packs and put them on shelf.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn-outline-white">Discuss your 2027 promo plan →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHY ELITEZ -->
<section class="section fade-up">
  <div class="label">Why Elitez</div>
  <h2>THE ONLY VENDOR THAT ASSEMBLES <span style="color:var(--orange)">AND DEPLOYS</span></h2>
  <p class="lead">Packaging companies in Singapore don't do field activation. Activation agencies don't do pack assembly. Elitez is the only vendor that bridges both — brief us once and we build the pack, put it on shelf, and report back.</p>
  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-card fade-up">
      <div class="why-num">01</div>
